ck:** payments-worker is back on v3.3.0, its most recent healthy production release, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. A human approver signed off on the rollback. The worker now reports healthy, and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 on payments-worker, and on-call has been paged. The incident notes that payments-api errors are expected to be downstream of the worker.\n- **Problem:** payments-api (v5.1.0) is still degraded, with an 18% error rate. I checked right after the rollback, so it may just need time to recover. But it could also mean the API's own v5.1.0 deploy is part of the problem.\n\nPlease check payments-api again in a few minutes. If it's still unhealthy, I can roll it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy production release. I haven't done that since you said to roll back only the worker.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TL8dtRUqk1HabAvbda4Vvt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0151Nxypmhrm8wXMSdooeXge", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_019pWJWso7fKw5zkggcjGLu6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SFMndZVTzPkstDLmwQ8A3R", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0162hUuPnCJxkWhsRHdnFv99", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"